[B] the seven weights of the fundamental G2 representation
  the 7-rep has 7 weights (6 short roots + 0).
  the 6 nonzero weights sit at 60-degree spacing (a hexagon) + centre —
  ordinary addition of weights does not implement Fano XOR.
  counterexample: 2w is not a weight for nonzero short weight w.
  short-weight angles: [0, 60, 120, 180, 240, 300]  (hexagon = 6-fold, the planets' ring)

[C] WEYL(G2): order twelve, preserving alternating root lengths
  |Weyl(G2)| = 12; rotational subgroup C6, no order-four rotation.
  Aut of the uncoloured twelve-cycle has order 24; these groups differ.

==========================================================================
VERDICT: the selected G2 representation and root system have counts 7
and 12. The angular relation has a checked correspondence; semantics
and empirical prediction do not follow from these counts.

[D] ASPECTS (harmonic divisions) as ANGLES BETWEEN G2 ROOTS
  short-short angles: [60, 120, 180]   (sextile 60, trine 120, opposition 180)
  short-long  angles: [30, 90, 150]   (semisextile 30, square 90, quincunx 150)
  These are angular classes. Calling them tension/ease is an additional
  interpretation, not a consequence of root length or the Weyl action.

[E] ELEMENTS (x3 modalities) — the 4+3 split on the 12-wheel
  every 90 deg (a square = a MODALITY, cardinal/fixed/mutable): ['Aries', 'Cancer', 'Libra', 'Capricorn']
  every 120 deg (a trine = an ELEMENT, fire/earth/air/water):  ['Aries', 'Leo', 'Sagittarius']
  -> modalities = order-4 rotations (square), elements = order-3 (trine):
     Z/12 = Z/4 x Z/3: four element classes of size three and
     three modality classes of size four. A cyclic step is (+1,+1).
     The order-four rotation belongs to C12, not to Weyl(G2).

[F] the separate finite Fano incidence structure
  Aut of the compact real octonions is G2. The seven nonzero grades
  in F2^3 form Fano points, with incidence automorphism group GL(3,2),
  of order 168. This preserves a specified discrete incidence relation.
  Reducing signs modulo two does not identify this group with the full
  automorphism group of an octonion algebra in characteristic two.
  See symbolica_role_transport.py for exact role/action preservation.
